From f91a40e595b746a102fea446e733cdf370effe18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:30:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(dlssnr): denoise first with display-resolution motion
 vectors (DX12)

Denoise first refused games whose upscaler is created without MVLowRes
(e.g. Stellar Blade), because its private 1:1 DLSS/RR pass and NR run at
render resolution. Resample the game's display-resolution vectors into a
private render-sized RG32F texture each frame instead:

- nearest output texel under each render pixel centre (no edge blending),
  read from the MV subrect origin over the DLSS output extent
- values converted to render pixels (MV scale * render / output per axis);
  the 1:1 pass, private SR step and NR then use MV scale 1 with MVLowRes
- jitter offsets unchanged; game motion read in its declared state and
  restored; private copy rests readable and lives in the GPU-retired
  denoise-first generation
- the game's own upscaler keeps its original inputs; render-resolution
  games keep the previous passthrough path

New shader dlssnr_motion_downscale.hlsl (dxc cs_6_0, signed DXIL), planning
helper DlssNr_DisplayMotion.h, headless unit test and a WARP test that runs
the shipped DXIL.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KksEgLpWVJEmw2R46xQgz1
